learnings:
  - Mid-stream agent termination is recoverable when the call site is in place and the helper signature is inferable from the call — a focused recovery prompt with explicit 'completed/missing' diff lets the next agent close the gap quickly
  - tsup/esbuild does NOT catch undefined function references at build time — a successful build is not proof that runtime won't ReferenceError. Always grep for definitions when the call site was scaffolded but the helper was the next-up todo.
  - preAction hook on commander program is the right place to gate cross-cutting CLI behavior (migration notices) — short-circuited by --version/--help automatically
